  "findings": [
    "Guide omission: deploy/compose/PREBUILT.md says to create the Skill's binding through Skills but not that the binding is a second governed change needing the same reviewer and second-administrator approval. Corrected on main with this record.",
    "Console defect: Recent context lists every run as '0 tokens · 0 selections'. GET /v1/context-runs deliberately blanks those counts in listings (ContextRunView::for_listing); the console renders the blanks as values.",
    "Console wording: a run that advertised a Skill reports 'Some context detail is unavailable under current policy' and hides its token count and Skills on later reads. The gateway withholds authored detail by design because Skill advertisements cannot be re-authorised from the run row; the message attributes this to policy."
  ],
  "limits": "Agent-run on an existing host; not an unfamiliar engineer's guide-only trial. Plain-Compose route, not the ./synveda-compose launcher. No native client, harness, model or provider use. Lexical-only retrieval as shipped.",
  "cleanup": "Final ordinary docker compose down left no project containers or networks and retained the installation, postgres-data and browser-acceptance-state volumes with their keys. Unrelated projects and the fixed synveda-evaluation volumes were not touched."
